    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22628" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incŭbĭto</span></b> ,
			āre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. freq.</i> [incubo], <i>to lie
				in</i> or <i>upon</i> any thing: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cellae, in quibus incubitant,</span>”
				<i>in which they brood</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					8, 14, 9</span></i>
			. In <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 43, 68, § 169</span></i>, the
			best read. is in cubitu.—In mal. part.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jam incubitatus es,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Pers. 2, 4, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
